# =====================================================
# ROBLOX CHEAT SCANNER v5.8
# PROPERTY OF JD
#
# v5.8 -- CAPTURE TABLE LISTS EVERYTHING
#   * The Hidden-from-screen-capture table now names every process, always.
#     Name resolution goes through four routes (Get-Process, WMI, the resolved
#     image path, then the PID itself) so a row is never blank and never
#     dropped. A window whose owner cannot be identified is MORE interesting
#     than one that can, so it stays in the table with the gaps labelled.
#   * Empty title, empty class, missing signer and unreachable path each print
#     what is missing in place, rather than rendering as an empty cell that
#     reads like "nothing there".
#   * When the section did not run at all the table says NOT CHECKED with the
#     reason, instead of "no windows are excluded".
#
# v5.8 -- THIRD-PARTY ANTIVIRUS
#   * FIXED (false positive on every Norton/McAfee/Bitdefender machine):
#     Windows puts Defender into PASSIVE mode when another antivirus registers.
#     Get-MpComputerStatus then reports AntivirusEnabled = False, and v5.6
#     raised "Defender antivirus: DISABLED" as a finding. It now identifies the
#     active product first and records passive Defender as context. A genuine
#     "no protection at all" case is still flagged.
#   * NEW: Security Products section. Enumerates every AV, antispyware and
#     firewall product registered with Windows Security Center
#     (root\SecurityCenter2), decodes productState into on/off plus definition
#     freshness, and prints the raw hex so a reviewer can verify it by hand.
#     No product registered at all is CRITICAL.
#   * NEW: honest coverage reporting. A third-party product's detection history
#     cannot be read -- no common API, proprietary formats per vendor. The
#     Defender threat-history check is now reported as NOT APPLICABLE on those
#     machines rather than returning empty and reading as clean.
#
# v5.8 -- REPORT REBUILT AROUND REVIEWER QUESTIONS
#   * HTML report regrouped into seven categories named after the question a
#     reviewer is asking, not after how the scanner is built. Groups with
#     findings open automatically; quiet groups collapse to one line. Empty
#     tables no longer render at all.
#   * "Hidden from screen capture" is now its own top-level category AND its
#     own tab, listing EVERY capture-excluded window including trusted ones,
#     with a live filter, an untrusted-only toggle and a mismatch-only toggle.
#   * NEW: name/signer mismatch rule. An unsigned binary called
#     RobloxPlayerBeta.exe still reads NotSigned; system binary names running
#     from outside System32 are flagged the same way.
#   * File paths are their own clickable field after a pipe separator: click to
#     copy, or open the containing folder. Resolved through three routes
#     (Get-Process, WMI, QueryFullProcessImageName) and reported as
#     "could not reach" when all three fail, never as a blank cell.
#   * NEW: browser history clearing. Chromium records
#     browser.last_clear_browsing_data_time in Preferences and it survives the
#     clear itself. Firefox has no equivalent, so profile creation is reported
#     as context instead.
#   * Report themes: purple (default), green, blue. Severity colours are fixed
#     across all three -- red and amber are the only colours carrying meaning.
#
# v5.8 -- DEFENDER DETECTIONS NOW NAME THE FILE
#   v5.4 printed the threat name and a raw status number and threw the path
#   away, so a reviewer could not tell WHICH file Defender hit. Each detection
#   now resolves and prints:
#       file    - the path, with \Device\HarddiskVolumeN mapped to a drive letter
#       [STILL ON DISK] - checked live; forces CRITICAL regardless of status
#       sha256  - hashed if present, so it can go straight into -HashList
#       inside  - the archive it was extracted from
#       from    - the URL it was downloaded from (webfile resources)
#       ran as  - PID, if it executed
#       cmd     - the command line, for behavioural detections
#   Status IDs are resolved to names (3 = Quarantined, 103 = REMOVE FAILED,
#   5 = Allowed by user, ...) instead of bare numbers, and the scan ends with a
#   summary of every detected file still present.
#
# v5.8 -- FIXES FROM THE FIRST v5.3 RUN
#   * FIXED (silent, total): the PE import parser failed on EVERY 64-bit
#     binary. [uint64]0x8000000000000000 parses as Int64 in PowerShell 5.1,
#     overflows negative, and the cast threw inside a catch. Every call
#     returned Ok=$false, so "PE Signatures: 0 parsed" was reported as a clean
#     pass and CAPTURE-PE-01 / EXTMEM-PE-01 never ran once. Parse failures are
#     now counted and reported as NOT CHECKED instead of silence.
#   * FIXED: the scanner flagged ITSELF as a renamed cheat binary. The exe
#     embeds this script, which contains the cheat term list, so it matched
#     "synapse" inside its own dictionary. Self-marker detection now excludes
#     the tool from the renamed-binary, PE and config scans.
#   * FIXED: ANTENNA-CFG-01 fired on a saved text file containing ordinary
#     Roblox words. Markers are now split STRONG (engine-internal offset names)
#     vs WEAK (common vocabulary); weak names alone can no longer fire.
#   * REMOVED two dead section registrations left over from the v5.1 rename
#     that reported NOT CHECKED with a blank reason.
#
# v5.8 -- PE BEHAVIOUR SIGNATURES
#   Built from a confirmed sample. The import-hash implementation here was
#   verified to reproduce the standard pefile imphash exactly.
#
#     PE-IMPHASH-01  import hash on the blocklist. Survives renaming and
#                    cosmetic recompiles -- only changing which APIs the
#                    program calls changes it.
#     CAPTURE-PE-01  binary imports SetWindowDisplayAffinity. Fires from disk
#                    even when the cheat is CLOSED, so shutting it down before
#                    a scan no longer hides it. This is the single most
#                    important rule for a league that verifies by screenshare.
#     EXTMEM-PE-01   external read-only cheat profile: reads another process's
#                    memory + walks its modules + synthesises input + draws a
#                    layered/D3D overlay, but NEVER writes or injects. Invisible
#                    to module-enumeration and injection checks by design.
#     EXTMEM-PE-02   reads AND writes process memory (trainer/debugger) - REVIEW
#     DRIVER-PE-01   unsigned binary with DeviceIoControl + process access
#     ANTENNA-CFG-02 settings file matched on ESP/aimbot feature keys
#
#   ANTENNA-CFG-01 offset markers replaced with field names taken from a
#   confirmed sample, so an offset dump is identified by CONTENT -- the cheat's
#   own instructions tell users to rename the file to anything.
#
#   -HashList now accepts imphashes (32 hex chars) alongside SHA256 (64).
#
# v5.8 -- NAMED SIGNATURES
#   Every rule now carries an ID, so a disputed finding can be looked up and
#   argued with by hand instead of resting on "the scanner said suspicious".
#     ANTENNA-REG-01/02  cheat config key under HKCU + its offsets_path value
#     ANTENNA-CFG-01     Roblox offset dump matched by CONTENT, not filename
#     ANTENNA-NET-01     offset-distribution host in the DNS cache
#     OVERLAY-WIN-01     topmost + layered + click-through window, untrusted owner
#     OVERLAY-WIN-02     ImGui/overlay window class
#     EXTMEM-PROC-01     unsigned process holding a READ-ONLY handle to Roblox
#
# v5.8 -- ANTI-SCREENSHARE COUNTERMEASURES
#   * NEW: screen-capture evasion scan. Enumerates every top-level window and
#     checks GetWindowDisplayAffinity. A window set to WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE
#     is drawn on the monitor but omitted from OBS, Discord, screenshots and
#     remote desktop. Cheat overlays ship this as "streamproof" -- it is the
#     mechanism that defeats screenshare verification, and it was previously
#     invisible to every check in this tool. Trusted publishers (DRM players,
#     password managers) are context; unsigned owners are CRITICAL.
#   * NEW: cheat config + registry artifact scan. Overlay cheats keep settings
#     outside the binary so the exe can be renamed or re-downloaded. Those
#     artifacts survive deleting the exe and users rarely remove them:
#       - HKCU root keys named after known cheats (values printed)
#       - offsets.json / *_cfg.jsonc / autoload.cfg by name
#       - a "logs" folder sitting beside an unsigned executable
#   * Added "antenna" (Tier A) and offsets.imtheo.lol to the term/domain lists.
#
# v5.0
#   FIXED (real bug, visible in the v4.9 run as "BAM (0)"):
#     foreach ($x in (try {...} catch {...})) -- try/catch is a STATEMENT in
#     PowerShell 5.1, not an expression. In an enumerable position it yields
#     nothing, so the BAM loop never executed a single iteration and the tab
#     was empty on every scan ever run. Prefetch used a different code path,
#     which is why it showed 333 while BAM showed 0.
#
#   NEW:
#   * Dedicated BAM parser with its own pass, deliberately NOT filtered by the
#     selected scan window. The tab is a complete execution record (account,
#     exe, path, last run, tier); findings still come from the time-filtered
#     path. An empty BAM store is now itself a REVIEW finding.
#   * Windows install date + last boot + uptime in the banner, Status tab and
#     report header. An install less than 7 days old raises a REVIEW finding:
#     a reinstall erases every artifact this tool depends on, so a clean scan
#     on a fresh machine carries little weight.
#
#   UI:
#   * Findings and the HTML report are ordered Tier A -> B -> C -> untiered,
#     then by severity, then alphabetically.
#   * Prefetch tab sorts most-run-first, with the Runs column moved left.
#   * Timestamps render as "Aug 05, 2026 12:40:31 AM PDT" instead of bare
#     24-hour local time with no zone.
#   * Snapshot delta no longer prints every entry to the console -- 402 rows
#     buried the rest of the scan. Console gets counts and criticals; the
#     per-entry detail stays in the Delta tab.
#   * Status tab opens with the machine environment block.
#
# v5.8 -- FINAL
#   REMOVED:
#   * Roblox log file scanning. The markers it looked for appear in ordinary
#     client script errors, and the section produced no true positives across
#     six live runs.
#
#   ADDED (ported from the Tier 3 v6 lineage):
#   * Defender threat history (Get-MpThreatDetection). A first-party detection
#     is stronger evidence than any name match this tool produces. Active
#     detections are CRITICAL; remediated ones are REVIEW.
#   * AMSI bypass registry keys (AmsiEnable=0, per-user CLSID hijack).
#     Counting providers was not enough -- AMSI can be present but disabled.
#   * Defender ETW autologger presence.
#   * PowerShell script block logging status (context).
#   * AppInit_DLLs -- injects a DLL into every process linking user32.
#   * IFEO Debugger hijack -- running program X silently launches binary Y.
#   * Event 104 (System log cleared). Previously only 1102 (Security) was read.
#   * Windows build, activation state and shadow copy count in the report header.
#
# v5.8 -- MEMORY SUBSYSTEM
#   * NEW: MEM_MAPPED executable regions are now detected. v4.5-v4.7 examined
#     PRIVATE memory only, so section-mapped injection (NtCreateSection +
#     NtMapViewOfSection) was structurally invisible -- and that technique is
#     used precisely because PRIVATE-only scanners cannot see it.
#   * NEW: injection-host scan (explorer, rundll32, dllhost, regsvr32, mshta,
#     wscript, cscript, notepad). STRUCTURAL ONLY -- unbacked/mapped executable
#     memory and anomalous thread entry points. Deliberately NOT string
#     matching: explorer holds the path of every file the user has browsed, so
#     string-scanning it (as Tier 3 v6 did) flags files merely SEEN in a folder.
#   * RWX private regions are now CRITICAL rather than a flat REVIEW.
#   * Region type (IMAGE / MAPPED / PRIVATE) is reported per finding. Every
#     memory hit previously claimed "PRIVATE" regardless of where it came from.
#   * Hollowing check reports WHICH condition tripped, and adds the
#     not-committed case.
#   * Coverage line now distinguishes string coverage (a fraction of PRIVATE)
#     from executable-region coverage (all regions).
#
# v4.7
#   RESTORED (dropped in the v4.5 rewrite, absent for four builds):
#   * Renamed-binary scan. Reads cheat strings from inside a PE's first 64KB
#     instead of trusting its filename. v4.5 kept the helper and never called
#     it, so solara.exe renamed to svchost.exe defeated every check at once.
#   * All-time prefetch pass. The main pass honours the selected time range, so
#     a participant accepting the 2-day default hid anything older. This pass
#     ignores the range.
#   * Recent files (.lnk) -- presence class.
#   * Generic-named unsigned executables in temp -- now needs elevated entropy
#     AND no valid signature, and caps at REVIEW.
#
#   NEW:
#   * Recycle Bin $I records: original path + deletion time of deleted files.
#     Nothing evicts these automatically, unlike prefetch.
#   * Browser download history (Chrome/Edge/Brave/Opera/Firefox). Survives the
#     file being deleted, which Zone.Identifier does not. Raw string scan, not
#     a SQLite parse -- flagged REVIEW, never Critical, and the report says so.
#
#   FIXED:
#   * Bulk-deletion false positive introduced in v4.6. Any large removal was
#     CRITICAL, so Storage Sense trimming 86 of the OLDEST prefetch entries --
#     including Defender's own binaries -- read as anti-forensic cleanup.
#     Removals are now profiled: if the deleted set is full of Windows
#     servicing binaries it is CONTEXT; selective removal stays CRITICAL.
#   * Renamed $profile to $delProfile in the delta comparison; $profile is a
#     PowerShell automatic variable.
#
# v4.6.1
#   * GUI: every tab now has a detail pane. Clicking a row shows all columns in
#     full, including Evidence -- which is the column that gets clipped and the
#     one carrying the caveats that stop a finding being misread.
#   * GUI: horizontal scrolling made explicit, selection stays visible when the
#     grid loses focus, Ctrl+C copies the selected row.
#
# v4.6
#   * NEW: bulk/total artifact removal between scans is now CRITICAL on its own.
#     Per-item deletions were Context, so losing 28 prefetch entries and the
#     entire Shimcache in 13 minutes would have scored as nothing.
#   * FIXED: executor PRODUCT names in client memory were filed as grey context
#     alongside ordinary chat vocabulary. They are now REVIEW, with a note when
#     the string is short enough to occur by chance in binary data.
#   * NEW: an empty AppCompatCache is CRITICAL, not a quiet SKIP.
#   * NEW: baselines are archived to .\cheat_scan_baselines\ before being
#     overwritten. Previously every run destroyed the prior state.
#   * FIXED: declining the delta prompt left the section reason blank.
#
# v4.5.4 (patch)
#   * RESTORED: scanner self-hash (banner, report meta grid, report footer).
#     A SHA256 digest is one-way and identical on every machine running the same
#     build -- it identifies the CODE, never the operator. When the script is
#     pasted into a console instead of run from disk it now says UNAVAILABLE and
#     warns, rather than printing a placeholder that looked like a value.
#
# v4.5.3 (patch)
#   * REMOVED: scanner self-hash (was printed in the banner, the report meta
#     grid, and the report footer). Build identity now comes from the version
#     string alone. The REPORT hash is unaffected and still printed.
#
# v4.5.2 (patch)
#   * FIXED (regression from v4.5.1): the AmCache console line still referenced
#     $props after the RegistryKey rewrite, printing blank name/path.
#   * Baseline integrity warning now names the missing sidecar file.
#
# v4.5.1 (patch) -- fixes found by the first live v4.5 run:
#   * FIXED: the HTML report helper was named H(), which collides with the
#     built-in alias h -> Get-History. Aliases resolve BEFORE functions, so
#     every cell in the report called Get-History with a file path. Renamed
#     to HtmlEnc(). This is why v4.5 spewed ParameterBindingException.
#   * FIXED: AmCache hive never unmounted. The PowerShell registry PROVIDER
#     caches open key handles that GC will not release; now uses the
#     RegistryKey API with explicit Close/Dispose.
#   * FIXED: Get-WinEvent throws when a log has no matching events. Event 1102
#     reported "unavailable" (a coverage gap) when it meant "none found".
#   * NEW: mid-scan Roblox process drift is detected and reported. In the first
#     v4.5 run the client restarted between sections, so different sections
#     examined different process instances without saying so.
#
# CHANGES FROM v4.4 -- see CHANGELOG.md for the full list.
#
# HEADLINE CHANGES:
#   * Numeric scores REMOVED. Replaced with 4-state status:
#       CRITICAL (red) / REVIEW (amber) / CLEAR (green) / NOT CHECKED (grey)
#     A section that could not run now reports NOT CHECKED, never CLEAR.
#   * Term list is TIERED. Tier A = cheat-only (scores). Tier B = dual-use
#     (shown, never escalates alone). Tier C = fragment (shown, never scores).
#     Nothing was deleted from the term list.
#   * Matching is path-TOKENISED with word boundaries, and the user-profile
#     prefix is stripped, so a username can never match a term.
#   * NEW: loaded-module signer check, Zone.Identifier download provenance,
#     WER crash artifacts, launcher Modifications folder, SHA256 blocklist.
#   * Prefetch is now MAM-decompressed (run counts actually work).
#   * Handle enumeration parser fixed (was reading garbage on x64).
#
# INSTRUCTIONS:
#   FIRST SCAN  -- Close Roblox completely before running
#   SECOND SCAN -- Open Roblox, join a game, wait 1-3 min, run again
#
# Run as Administrator in PowerShell 5.1
# =====================================================

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [switch]$Unattended,
    [ValidateSet('2','3','7','all')]
    [string]$Days,
    [string]$HashList,
    [string]$BaselinePath,
    [string]$OutputDir
)

$isAdmin = ([Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal][Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent()).IsInRole([Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]"Administrator")
if (-not $isAdmin) {
    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "  ======================================" -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "  ERROR: NOT RUNNING AS ADMINISTRATOR"   -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "  ======================================" -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "  Right-click PowerShell -> Run as Administrator" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    if (-not $Unattended) { Start-Sleep 5 }
    exit 1
}

if ($PSVersionTable.PSVersion.Major -ge 6) {
    Write-Host "  ERROR: This script targets Windows PowerShell 5.1." -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "  You are running PowerShell $($PSVersionTable.PSVersion)." -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

[Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8
$OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing

